            For most softwood decks, a semi-transparent penetrating oil such as Armstrong Clark or Ready Seal is the right call: it protects against sun and water, fades instead of peeling, and recoats with a wash and a single thin coat. Choose DEFY Extreme if you want water-based, TWP if mildew is your main enemy, Cabot for hardwoods and a solid stain only for a deck that is past showing off its grain.
          </p>
